# What EAS Build is allowed to upload.
#
# Without this file, EAS copies the archive "starting from the root of the git
# repository" — so an Android build was shipping backend/, web/, admin/ and
# docs/ to Expo's servers along with the app. None of it is used: mobile/ has no
# root package.json above it, no workspace, and no parent-relative dependency.
# It was 417 MB per build, most of it admin/src-tauri/target.
#
# ── Read this before editing ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The moment this file exists, EAS stops honouring EVERY .gitignore in the repo.
# Not just the root one — all of them. So anything that must not be uploaded has
# to be re-listed here even though git already ignores it, and the consequences
# of forgetting are not academic: mobile/ contains an Android keystore and a
# .env, both of which git excludes and neither of which belongs in a build
# archive.
#
# `.git` and `node_modules` are excluded by EAS itself and need no rule.
#
# It must live at the git repository root — EAS does not look anywhere else,
# which is why this sits beside backend/ rather than inside mobile/.

# ── Everything outside the app ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/*
!/mobile/

# ── Credentials. Re-listed because this file disabled mobile/.gitignore ─────
# The keystore is already held by EAS as a build credential; a second copy
# riding along inside the archive is exposure with nothing bought for it.
mobile/*.jks
mobile/*.p8
mobile/*.p12
mobile/*.key
mobile/*.mobileprovision
mobile/.env
mobile/.env.*
!mobile/.env.example

# ── Build output and local state ────────────────────────────────────────────
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/
mobile/web-build/
mobile/expo-env.d.ts
mobile/.kotlin/
mobile/*.orig.*

# ── Not part of the app ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prompts and notes for producing the kitten clips. The clips themselves live
# in assets/ and are shipped; this is the paperwork behind them.
mobile/design/
mobile/.claude/
